 "version": "0.1",
 "notes": "Curated emotion typography table (0.9). Option 1 of each emotion is canonical for an explicit emotion; exploration level 0 without --emotion keeps the 0.8 tone pairings (legacy). Every option also loads `fallback_face` for glyph fallback (₹ € digits). `substitutes`: a missing face file is replaced role-wise by its substitute (recorded in fallback_from as '<option>:<from>-><to>'); Necto Mono (Collletttivo) -> IBM Plex Mono until bundled. Face `class` (grotesk|condensed|geometric|serif|slab|sans|mono|hand) drives the typography_style category constraint (docs/TYPOGRAPHY.md). (0.24 M8) Faces carry motion metadata: contrast, width, and x_height (x over H glyph height) + tabular_digits measured from the file (test motion_type). `pairings` = library v2 (level 1 draws only from these via `usage[genre][tone]`, filtered by use_for.temperaments); every pairing and every level>=1 emotion option must pass motion_safe (docs/TYPOGRAPHY.md).",
